  "scientific_review": [
    "All four Caribbean/Azores January15/July15,2022 cases retain every one of20 original anchors with exact source positions, raw-profile/diagnosis pointers and primary depths/spans. Unselected,edge/support-edge and censored cases remain explicit; fully unsupported cases stay unresolved.",
    "Eleven cloud projection tests verify source values, frames/gates/cutoffs, original anchors and gaps, unselected geometry, adjacent-only interpolation, mutations and pin/count integrity, preservation of all96 previous scenarios,old CSV cells,ownership,immutable v14 base and thirteen old addenda, and no physical/annual promotion. Six baseline tests pass on the same exact code commit. Source collection separately passed40 checks and audited all original sections. Earlier WSC auxiliary report remains pinned.",
    "Both use primary10cm/s andsurface>5cm/s with complete finite0–200m signed-integral selection. Caribbean uses270degree westward and Azores90degree eastward through depth. First southern native tie wins. Gate/support-edge maxima stay unresolved without weaker interior substitution; sensitivities share the selected column. No thermal gate is used.",
    "Caribbean68–80W/12–16.5N is a partial southern-jet-context reach. A separate northern jet, western northward deflections, upstream passages,Yucatan/Loop and detached eddies are not represented as target entities. Richardson2005 drifters provide regional branch context, not2022 velocity/depth validation. Existing RU29_2024 inversion-derived layers and15cm/s sensitivity keep their own dates, methods and source uncertainty. These cases neither relabel nor independently validate them.",
    "Azores35–21W/31.5–36.5N is a partial eastward jet reach. Comas-Rodriguez2011 distinguishes surface-intensified eastward Azores from subsurface westward countercurrent; the source2009 density-layer extent around2000m is not a model lower boundary. Volkov/Fu2011 mean jet tilt supplies geography rather than an imposed instantaneous axis or speed. Countercurrent,recirculation,Portugal/Canary continuation and eddies remain separate target identities.",
    "All gates/stops are exploratory OSW choices rather than digitized axes, full widths, route lengths or uncertainty bounds. Geographic maxima do not independently establish named-current or branch membership. Mesoscale flow and connected same-sign neighboring currents can affect these layers; missing,dry,bed or domain limits censor rather than fill a current bottom.",
    "All field acquisition,retries,selection,geometry/contour calculations and tests ran sequentially in cloud on one idle CPU. Local work was code preparation,primary text/metadata review,hash checks and exact artifact retention. No local numerical field processing/tests or runtime/UI/browser work occurred. Frozen sources/operators/helpers and byte/transport caps remain unchanged.",
    "Only adjacent original eligible nodes permit assumed interpolation; no skipping gaps,extrapolation,alternate-cutoff fill or weaker interior substitution. Upper/lower/span stay distinct and paired spans require both boundaries. Unselected midpoint geometry is explicitly unsampled; connectors are not measured current lengths. Two snapshots do not establish annual/seasonal ranges,physical thickness,matched areas,volumes,state joins or global sums. Inventoryv14 adds one pinned addendum/CSV; previous data,canonical register and eddy baseline remain unchanged. Current coverage,observational/seasonal validation and query/runtime integration remain unfinished."
  ],
